# End-to-end characterisation check, run inside real ChimeraX.
#
#   ChimeraX --nogui --silent --exit --script tests/integration/characterise_1brs.cxc
#
# The host-light suite cannot reach anything that needs the ChimeraX SASA
# engine, so buried area, %NIS, dG, Kd and the per-residue hot-spot ranking are
# unverified there. Those are exactly the numbers the manuscript still quotes
# from a one-off session, so this file exists to regenerate them on demand and
# to prove the whole stack still runs against a real structure.
#
# Expected, from tests/unit/core/test_golden_1brs.py (already locked):
#   interface 4.5 A ....... 19 + 16 residues, 43 contacts
#   affinity contacts ..... 68 at 5.5 A, binned CC 11 / AC 25 / PP 2 / AP 11
#   salt bridges .......... 4, including the Asp39 triad
# Expected, from the cross-validation session (this run confirms them):
#   buried area ........... 1129 A^2
#   dG .................... -10.63 kcal/mol
#
# Export is deliberately absent: it is covered by molcompose_smoke.cxc, and
# offscreen rendering is not guaranteed in a headless session.

close all
open 1brs

molcompose capabilities model #1
molcompose interface A D model #1 distance 4.5
molcompose interactions model #1
molcompose buriedarea model #1
molcompose affinity model #1
molcompose hotspots model #1

# The one-call path must agree with the individual commands above, and must
# list confidence as skipped: 1BRS is X-ray and its B-factor column is not
# pLDDT, so a number there would be a scientific error, not a bug.
molcompose characterise A D model #1

molcompose report /private/tmp/molcompose-1brs-report.md model #1 format md

# NOTE: `molcompose confidence model #1` is deliberately NOT run here. It raises
# a UserError on this structure -- which is the correct behaviour -- and a
# UserError aborts the rest of a .cxc script. The refusal is covered by the unit
# tests and is visible in the `skipped` field of the characterise summary above.
